<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.390
Another Member In The Family

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.310
<i>On the Alm mountain, it is already
summer through and through.</i>

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:36.320
<i>Today, as always, Heidi goes with Peter
towards the mountain pasture.</i>

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:42.350
Peter, hurry up!

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.100
Very well.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.100
{+++MJN She is adapting well to
the life in the mountains.}From the looks of it, she seems to have
adjusted to life on the mountain.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.460
Don't you think, Joseph?

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.650
{++++MJN You're so quiet.}Ha ha ha, unsociable fellow!

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.240
Look! That cloud looks like a goat.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.910
Now it looks more like Joseph.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.940
Hey, let's eat.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.060
But we've just arrived.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.560
But it smells so good.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.090
{++++MJN Don't be a glutton.
It's still early.}Always thinking about food!
It's still early.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.840
Snowflake! There's some sweet grass over here.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:21.940
See?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:29.980
Heidi!

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.120
Grab my hat!

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.610
It went your way!

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:53.600
Heidi!

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.710
We must seek shelter!
Hurry up!

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.550
But we didn't even eat yet!

00:03:58.790 --> 00:03:59.980
There's a storm coming!

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:02.730
Come on, let's go!

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.320
What's happening?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.220
A storm! It's a storm!

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.240
Is that a storm?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.500
It's far away.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.680
But it's coming here.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.410
Peter!

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.320
Peter!

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.280
Are we all right?
Are we going to be all right?

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.320
I don't know!
Come on, let's go!

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.850
It started to rain!
Let's go!

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.550
Peter Is with her.
I don't need to worry.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.480
Heidi, hurry up!

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.480
{++++MJN The rain feels good.}Ah, it feels nice and cold.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.390
{+++MJN You'll catch a cold!}If you stand around, you'll catch a cold!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.920
Look, the shelter is already there!

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.300
What a relief.
Then we'll be fine.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.010
We're faster than the lightning.
It can't catch us.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:19.660
Heidi!

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:21.240
Peter!

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.920
Are you cold?

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.790
Don't worry! Now we are safe from the
lightning and the rain.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:54.610
Really?

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.440
It's not over yet!

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:04.310
<i>For Heidi, this is once
again a new experience.</i>

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:06.640
<i>The rightfulness of nature's changes,</i>

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.020
<i>and that the mountain's weather
sometimes changes suddenly,</i>

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:11.980
<i>are things she experiences for the first time.</i>

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.640
The storm is over.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.040
Come on, it's over.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:31.170
It's so quiet.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.340
{++++MJN}What's this?

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.270
{++++MJN}It's crying.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:49.600
{***Timing++++MJN}What is?

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.670
{++++MJN It's coming from there!}It's coming from over there!

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.770
{++++MJN Peter, it's a little bird!}Oh no, oh no! Peter!
It's a baby bird!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.350
Poor thing. It's all wet.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.500
It must have fallen during the storm.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.960
{++++MJN Let's eat it!}Let's eat it, it looks tasty.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:22.070
No!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.760
Let's go home!

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:33.710
All right?

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.610
It stopped raining, so the goats still...

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.210
I'm going home.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.750
Why?

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.890
I want to feed the little bird.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.240
{++++MJN He's too small, he won't live.}It's so weak, there's no
way it will grow up.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:50.610
{++++MJN He will.}It will!

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:52.320
{++++MJN No, he won't.}Yeah right!

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.470
{++++MJN Yes, he will!}I'll raise it!

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.740
I'm going home alone.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:01.700
Heidi!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.050
Snowflake, it's not time to leave yet!

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:09.440
Snowflake!

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:37.530
I'm back, Grandfather!

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.350
{++++MJN Were you scared?}Ah, I bet you were surprised by the rain.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.780
Look! Look what I found!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.250
{++++scared}Did the lightning scare you?

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:48.730
Look what I found.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:54.860
{++++MJN It's a small Goldfinch.}That's a baby finch.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.940
{++++MJN He was wet and shivering with cold.}He got soaked in the rain and fell to the ground.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:01.160
{++++MJN So that's why you brought him here!}Hmm, so that's why you came home at this time.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.910
{++++MJN Poor thing, don't you think?}You feel sorry for him, too, don't you?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.590
Stop, Joseph. You can't eat him!

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.740
Grandfather, I want to take care of him.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:16.690
You?

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:19.650
{++++MJN Yes, but will he be all right?}Yes! But do you think he'll live?

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:21.290
Let me see.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.100
He is very weak.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.270
He will survive, won't he, Grandfather?

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:30.670
I wonder.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:32.540
Yes, he will!

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.530
I know. He must be hungry.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.120
What does he eat?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:44.740
{++++MJN He's very small, so he should
eat small Insects and seeds.}You feed a chick live food. In other words,
small living worms and such.

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:47.160
{++++MJNReally? Then I'm going to catch insects.}I see. I'll go get some worms!

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.560
That's right, he needs a house.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.060
Can I put him here?

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.360
Yes, you can.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.770
Wait a little.
I'm going to make you a bed.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:14.940
{++++MJN She's so happy.}She's completely engrossed.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:28.780
Here!

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.220
Eat!

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.420
Look, Snowflake! Cute, isn't he?

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:50.330
Snowflake!

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.990
Peter. You said he wasn't going
to survive, but look how well he is.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.180
He may die tomorrow.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.240
That's a lie!
That will not happen!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.560
Right, Grandfather?
He'll be fine, right?

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.930
The chick's not going to die, is he?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.710
Why do you look so worried?

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:20.120
But Peter says that he may die tomorrow!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:24.630
Hey, Peter! Stop saying those
things and go home right now!

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.360
I-I didn't say anything...

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:27.360
Then... Goodbye!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.510
She only cares about that bird.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.750
What are you doing?

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:54.910
{++++MJN Peter. Are you all right?}Peter! You got caught in the
rain today, didn't you?

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:59.830
How is the little girl up there?
Is she well?

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.310
She is fine.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:06.410
{++++MJN But I do not believe that
she feels happy up there!}She's getting enough to eat, right?

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:08.760
{++++MJN She is.}She's eating.

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.290
Tell me, what does she do up there?

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.560
Today she found a little bird.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.450
A little bird?

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.060
{-Then, see you later.}Well, see you tomorrow.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.480
Peter!

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.970
See? He didn't even
want to talk about her.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.310
Maybe the girl is not doing well.
Poor thing.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:16.730
Grandfather!

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.280
Grandfather.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:19.730
What is it?

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:23.540
He is alive. He did not die.
He survived.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:25.950
That's good to hear.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.630
{++++MJN He is chirping because he's hungry.
I'll go outside to catch insects.}He's crying, "Peep, peep!" and wants to eat.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.510
I'll have to bring him some worms quickly.

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:44.860
Peter!

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.850
He didn't die!

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:49.110
He didn't?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.280
Look, it's insects.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:52.710
{++++MJN It's for him to eat.}I just picked them up now.

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:59.150
Today I'm going to show
you another way.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:01.100
I can't go with you today.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:02.660
You can't?

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:05.220
I can't let Pichi alone.

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:06.340
Pichi?

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.920
It's his name. He is always saying
"pichi pichi", so he is Pichi.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.280
Pretty, don't you think?

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.330
What kind of name is that?!

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:18.890
Leave that bird alone and come with me.
All right?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.450
I'm not going today.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.340
Well, see if I care!

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:28.840
<i>Snowflake!</i>

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:37.600
I'm sorry, Snowflake.
Go with him.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.500
Snowflake!

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:39.710
Go!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.850
<i>Heidi and Peter have finally gotten into a fight.</i>

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:53.510
<i>But Heidi can only think about Pichi.</i>

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:57.260
I have to give breakfast to Pichi.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:03.660
It's good?

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:07.450
Do you still want more?

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.300
All right! Wait just a little.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.560
He ate it!

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.270
I wonder if he eats this!

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.620
Oh! Joseph!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.670
Y-you ate it!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:35.560
Grandfather, Joseph ate a snail!

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:39.360
He ate it! He ate it!
He ate that!

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:41.120
He ate a snail!

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:43.660
{++++MJN It's natural!}That's nothing to be surprised about.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.850
He loves snails.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:52.150
{++++MJN Pichis's alone.}Then, Pichi is also...

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:59.430
Y-y-you can't!
You can't eat Pichi!

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:15.060
Grandfather, Pichi needs a bird cage!

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:21.290
But I don't think he needs to be in one.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:23.160
But, Joseph...

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:24.870
Him?

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.100
Joseph wants to eat him.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.160
He doesn't want to do such a thing.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:32.820
Do not worry about him.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:34.400
But...

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.790
You'll be a little tight, but hang in there.

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:04.750
You mustn't be seen by Joseph!

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.690
I'll get something for you to eat.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.170
Pichi!

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:16.730
Joseph, don't eat him!
Don't eat him!

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:20.300
Pichi! Pichi!
Pichi, wait!

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:22.220
Pichi!

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.810
He's gonna burn himself!

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:39.250
You ate him!

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:41.050
Joseph!

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:43.230
Idiot, idiot, idiot!

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:45.390
Joseph, you idiot!

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.200
Pichi.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:04.410
Pichi.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:20.480
Joseph.

00:22:21.850 --> 00:22:24.400
Joseph can't climb the stairs.

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:34.220
Joseph! Joseph!

00:22:35.770 --> 00:22:37.530
Joseph!

00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:40.810
Joseph.

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:50.320
You saved him.
Joseph, you saved Pichi.

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:53.420
Isn't that true?

00:22:54.340 --> 00:22:55.640
Isn't that true?

00:22:57.760 --> 00:22:59.230
Thank you, Joseph.

00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:02.250
I'm sorry that I doubted you!

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:10.570
Joseph.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:18.500
<i>Heidi understands that the
normally unsociable Joseph</i>

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:23.250
<i>is really a gentle and intelligent dog.</i>

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:26.870
<i>To Grandfather and Heidi,
living in the mountain cabin,</i>

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:30.220
<i>Joseph is part of the family.</i>

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:35.890
<i>Nevertheless, it would be nice if the frail
chick grew up safely, wouldn't it?</i>

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:58.340
<i>Pichi, who, thanks to Heidi,
has completely recovered,</i>

00:23:58.380 --> 00:24:00.710
<i>can't stay still anymore.</i>

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:05.840
<i>Seeing Pichi like that, Heidi resolutely decides
to take him with her to the mountain.</i>

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:10.970
<i>On the mountain, Pichi flies around
as if beside himself with happiness.</i>

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:16.060
<i>Seeing Pichi like that, Heidi and
Peter also have a lot of fun.</i>

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:21.070
<i>However, above Pichi's head,
a terrifying hawk appears.</i>

00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:24.280
<i>Heidi and Peter also completely lose their heads.</i>

00:24:24.610 --> 00:24:27.100
<i>Next time:
The Burnt Letter</i>

00:24:27.130 --> 00:24:28.660
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

